      "name": "Warehouse Relocation Operations",
      "description": "Warehouse relocation operations: warehouse and distribution moves, warehouse load-outs, inbound unloads, transload staging, and restacking, run by trained, supervised, self-managed moving and warehouse teams that support contractors and project managers — a project-support service, not day-hire labor and not a labor listing. The work is planned around the site itself: access, floor space, staging, and equipment handling. Pricing basis, as published: quoted per job and agreed before dispatch, with no required contract duration, adjustable for scope, equipment, travel, and after-hours work agreed before dispatch. Standard Job Pricing, verbatim: Unload $8.00/CWT; Load $10.00/CWT; APU $12.00/CWT; Residential/Driver Meet $400–$425 per man. Deployment needs served, as published on the industrial page: planned, overflow, peak, weekend, vacation, and emergency. Markets served: warehousing, manufacturing, transportation and logistics, retail distribution, 3PL, healthcare, commercial furniture dealers, corporate offices, general contractors, educational facilities, and hospitality and hotel renovations. Conditional: where a warehouse job actually involves a high-mass asset of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs, that asset moves under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation with floor deflection analysis to L/360, as part of the same flat-rate job — only where such an asset is actually involved. Not published and not claimed for warehouse relocation: any deployed-equipment list; drayage or chassis scope; bonded or free-trade-zone scope; refrigerated or cold-chain scope; customs scope; racking teardown or reinstall within this warehouse-relocation scope (published as its own service, Warehouse Racking Relocation); a phasing offering; WMS or inventory-system integration; permits or engineering scope; debris or close-out scope.",
